{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775323553-evLZfB3r9IGqyWSzprrs","role":"assistant","created":1775323559,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to find the historical data on personal saving rates from 1950-1990 in this Treasury Bulletin document. The extracted text mentions that the personal saving rate is measured as \"Household Saving as a Percent of After-Tax Income.\"\n\nFrom what I've seen so far, the document mentions:\n- A post-Depression low of 2.9 percent in 1987\n- 4.6 percent in both 1989 and 1990\n- A long-term average of 6.7 percent\n\nBut I don't see the detailed historical data from 1950-1990 with specific yearly values. Let me search more systematically through the document.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_545d6df4c5654acaa6ecbf14","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"Household Saving\\|Personal Saving\\|saving rate\\|after-tax income\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1991_09.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
{"type":"message","message":{"id":"msg_0ee51dc2-1ebd-4af3-9ddd-05bb051781c5","role":"user","created":1775323559,"content":[{"type":"toolResponse","id":"call_545d6df4c5654acaa6ecbf14","toolResult":{"status":"success","value":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"335:Consumer spending has begun to improve as employment opportunities increased in May and the moderation of inflation has helped to restore real purchasing power. Purchases of services such as medical care, personal care, transportation, household operations, education, personal business, and recreation have held up well even during the recession. Retail sales of durable and nondurable goods, including new cars, have strengthened following the disappointing results of last winter. Future gains are likely to be relatively modest, however, because of the low personal saving rate, continued consumer reluctance to add more debt, and the sluggish pace of prospective job and income gains.\n566:Household Saving as a Percent of After-Tax Income, Through First Half 1991\n568:The personal saving rate rose from a post-Depression low of 2.9 percent in 1987 to 4.6 percent in both 1989 and 1990, but remained well below the 6.7-percent long-term average. Saving appeared to be rising in early 1990, averaging 4.9 percent in the first half of the year. However, in the second half it dropped to only 4.2 percent as the slowing economy and increasing inflation reduced real incomes. The rate dipped to 3.7 percent in the second quarter of 1991, allowing only a 4-percent average for the first half of the year.","annotations":{"priority":0.0}}],"structuredContent":{"stdout":"335:Consumer spending has begun to improve as employment opportunities increased in May and the moderation of inflation has helped to restore real purchasing power. Purchases of services such as medical care, personal care, transportation, household operations, education, personal business, and recreation have held up well even during the recession. Retail sales of durable and nondurable goods, including new cars, have strengthened following the disappointing results of last winter. Future gains are likely to be relatively modest, however, because of the low personal saving rate, continued consumer reluctance to add more debt, and the sluggish pace of prospective job and income gains.\n566:Household Saving as a Percent of After-Tax Income, Through First Half 1991\n568:The personal saving rate rose from a post-Depression low of 2.9 percent in 1987 to 4.6 percent in both 1989 and 1990, but remained well below the 6.7-percent long-term average. Saving appeared to be rising in early 1990, averaging 4.9 percent in the first half of the year. However, in the second half it dropped to only 4.2 percent as the slowing economy and increasing inflation reduced real incomes. The rate dipped to 3.7 percent in the second quarter of 1991, allowing only a 4-percent average for the first half of the year.","stderr":"","exit_code":0},"isError":false}}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
